From: oveRTOS <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mps2-an500: SysTick runs at the 25 MHz system clock

mps_timer.c programs SysTick from the core clock with MPS_SYSTICK_CLOCK,
which this board gives as 32 MHz. The AN500 system clock is 25 MHz, and
so is QEMU's mps2-an500, so every tick lasted 12.8 ms instead of 10 ms
and all kernel time ran 1.28x slow: a guest `sleep 20` took 25.6 s.

--- a/boards/arm/mps/mps2-an500/include/board.h
+++ b/boards/arm/mps/mps2-an500/include/board.h
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
  * Pre-processor Definitions
  ****************************************************************************/
 
-#define MPS_SYSTICK_CLOCK   (32 * 1000 * 1000)
+#define MPS_SYSTICK_CLOCK   (25 * 1000 * 1000)
 
 /****************************************************************************
  * Public Data
